body:
This is debatable so feel free to ignore it, but I find the boilerplate for visiting other sub-nodes of the function def a bit distracting. As currently written I believe it is necessary in order to insert the hint in the correct order, but you might consider maintaining that property by instead keeping a bit of extra state for a pending return type hint that gets inserted when the visitor leaves the function's parameters:

```rust
// In the visit_stmt match:
Stmt::FunctionDef(function) => {
    let position = function.parameters.end();
    if self.settings.return_types
        && self.range.contains_inclusive(position)
        && let Some(ty) = inlay_hint_return_type(&self.model, function)
    {
        self.pending_return_hint = Some((
            function.parameters.as_ref(),
            InlayHint::return_type(
                InlayHintImportContext {
                    db: self.db,
                    file: self.model.program_file(),
                    importer: &self.importer,
                },
                function,
                ty,
            ),
        ));
    }
}

// In the SourceOrderVisitor implementation:
fn leave_node(&mut self, node: AnyNodeRef<'a>) {
    if let AnyNodeRef::Parameters(parameters) = node
        && let Some((_, hint)) = self
            .pending_return_hint
            .take_if(|(expected, _)| std::ptr::eq(*expected, parameters))
    {
        self.hints.push(hint);
    }
}
```

In my opinion, that is clearer as to which nodes actually need special handling.

