body:
Playing around on this branch a little, I think only looking at class attributes may be too narrow here? I think we also want to use the superclass declaration to inform the type of the class-body default in cases like this:

```py
class Spam:
    def __init__(self):
        self.x: list[int] = [42]

class Eggs(Spam):
    x = []

def _2(obj: Eggs):
    reveal_type(obj.x) 
```

It's OK for this to be a followup, though it does look like it might have some implications for the design of this PR

